  "design": "The receive transform decodes each assembled H.264 frame with WebCodecs ahead of the browser playout buffer and hands pictures to the bounded presenter. The original frame always continues into the unchanged browser path, which stays live as fallback. Pictures older than 200ms from decode are not shown; 150ms without fresh pictures lends the display to the browser path; 5s or a decoder error retires direct decode. HEVC and browsers without the API stay on the browser path. Applies only with exact UI enabled, which stays off by default in the package.",
  "decisions": {
    "keep_double_decode": "Cost measured at about 0.05-0.08 browser cores. Dropping the browser path risks repeated keyframe requests and loses the live fallback, so it was not attempted.",
    "queue_depth_3": "Depth 2 lost clip FPS to arrival bursts; depth 4 gave back latency; depth 3 passes the FPS gates with most of the gain. Depth 3 and 4 latency comparison came from one bench run each before candidate 190.",
    "backlog_limit_60": "A limit of 8 failed every Chrome session with decode backlog at startup."
  },
